  "body": "## What changed\n\n`assets/posts/fanuc-lathe.cps`: the section end's C-axis live-tool branch returned before `afterOp()`, the function that writes the optional stop (M01), program stop (M00) and go-home asked after an operation. The ask was neither posted after the live section nor reset, so it came out after the NEXT section. The live branch now falls through to the one shared `afterOp()` call, so every section, turning or live, ends with its own ask. A refused live section (no live-tool words) still consumes its ask.\n\n## Reproduction (turning section, live cross drill asking the stop, turning section; test mill-turn `millturn-live.mch`)\n\nBefore (main 6f1adf06), program stop asked after the cross drill:\n```\nM9\nM1004\nM1002\nG99\n(OPERATION: Face two - G54)\n...\nM9\nM05\nM00            <- after Face two, not after the cross drill\nG28 U0 W0\n```\nOptional stop: the same, `M01` after Face two's `M05`. Go home: `G28 U0` / `G28 W0` after Face two's `M05`, and the program-end home then skipped as already done.\n\nAfter (golden `crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/fanuc-lathe/live_then_stop.nc`):\n```\nM9\nM1004\nM1002\nG99\nM01            <- end of the cross drill (M00 / G28 U0 + G28 W0 in the same place)\n(OPERATION: Face two - G54)\n...\nM9\nM05\nG28 U0 W0\nM30\n```\n\n## End-of-section order (live section)\n\n`G80` if open, `M9`, live spindle off (`live_tool.spindle_off`), C axis off (`c_axis_off`), `G99`, then the asked M01 / M00 / G28 U0 + G28 W0. The turning branch's order (coolant off, spindle stop, spindle-mode reset, stop words) with the live release words in the spindle-stop place: the driven tool is stopped and C released before an operator reaches in, and the home moves X and Z only, after C is released. No new codes: every word is the machine file's or one the post already wrote. Recorded in `docs/decisions/1188-live-section-after-op.md`.\n\n## Other early returns checked\n\n- `fanuc-lathe.cps` / `tormach-lathe.cps` `startPreamble` / `endPreamble`: only the `sectionOpen` guards; `tormach-lathe.cps` has no live branch and calls `afterOp()` on every section end - fine.\n- Mill posts `fanuc`, `haas`, `heidenhain`, `mazak`, `sinumerik`, `doosan-dnm`: no return before `afterOp()` - fine.\n- `tormach`, `carvera`, `tormach-plasma`: write no after-operation words and do not declare `afterModes`; the engine refuses a stop/home ask for them by name (seen in the new refusal goldens) - fine.\n\n## Goldens\n\nNo existing golden changes (all `crates/app/tests/golden` and `crates/post/tests/recorded/golden` byte-identical). New: recorded stream `live_then_stop.cnc` and its goldens in all 11 per-post suites (`fanuc-lathe/live_then_stop.nc`; the other ten are named refusals - no liveTooling / afterModes).\n\n## How tested\n\nPinning tests (`crates/post/tests/script_fanuc_lathe.rs`): `an_optional_stop_after_a_live_section_posts_at_its_end`, `a_program_stop_after_a_live_section_posts_at_its_end`, `a_go_home_after_a_live_section_posts_at_its_end` (each: the word after `M1004` and `M1002`, before the next section's first block, posted exactly once), `no_stop_asked_after_a_live_section_posts_no_stop`; the three asked-stop tests fail on main. Recorded case `live_then_stop` in every `script_*` suite plus `recorded_streams::live_then_stop_stream_is_current`.\n\nGate: `cargo test -p camcraft-post` (all suites), app `lathe_post`, `lathe_post_css`, `lathe_post_tormach`, `lathe_post_refusals`, `c_axis_live`, `c_axis_unwind`, `lathe_cycle_exit`, `conformance`, `golden_cl`, `solid_law_goldens` green; clippy `-D warnings` on camcraft-post + camcraft-app clean; `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` green on head f3c3c34a.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNot run on a real control. The live-tool codes of the test machine (M1001-M1004) are placeholders, not a builder's words.\n\nChangelog: Fanuc lathe post: an optional stop, program stop or go-home asked after a C-axis live-tool operation is posted at the end of that operation instead of after the next one\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1188\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
